# Merge behaviour for the two documentation trackers EVERY task appends to.
#
# The problem this solves, measured 2026-08-18: every task records a change
# note in `docs/SUMMARY.md` and `docs/TESTS.md`, so any two parallel branches
# touch the same region of the same two files and the merge sweep stops on a
# conflict. It halted three times in one evening and left five reviewed,
# published tasks unmerged for a day (dash-10, loop-02, brw-12, hlth-01,
# wrk-01), each resolved by hand.
#
# `merge=union` keeps BOTH sides of a conflicting hunk instead of writing
# conflict markers, so two branches that each append their own note line both
# land and neither note is lost.
#
# WHAT UNION CANNOT DO, and why the note shape matters more than this file:
# union resolves per LINE. Two branches that each grow the SAME line — the old
# habit of appending a sentence to a module's table row, where the longest row
# was 19,410 characters — do not get their two additions merged; they get the
# whole row duplicated. So this attribute is only half the fix. The other half
# is the rule in CLAUDE.md §12: a change note is ONE NEW LINE, and an existing
# line is never grown to record one. `autoloop/tests/test_docs_merge.py` pins
# both halves, including a test that demonstrates the duplication above.
#
# Deliberately exactly two paths. No wildcard, no `docs/*`, no source file:
# union never reports a conflict, so anything listed here loses genuine
# edit/edit conflict detection. That trade is acceptable for an append-only
# note ledger and is NOT acceptable for code — a real source conflict must
# still stop the sweep.
docs/SUMMARY.md merge=union
docs/TESTS.md merge=union
